# General Rules

Only unmodified retail copies of the game are allowed. Rules related to console modifications and the use of practice tools can be found [here](https://www.speedrun.com/sly1/forums/u27vn).

On PS4 and PS5, Enhancements must be set to Off in the emulator settings (accessible by pressing Options). The use of savestates is not permitted during the run.

Any action affecting the speedrun time, which results from using a cheat code, is banned.

# Versions

Runs that use PS4 v1.00 on a PS4 should be submitted as PS4 v1.0. Runs that use any other version should be submitted as Classic. 

Runs performed on PS5 must use v1.000.001 or later (PS5 version) or v1.01 or later (PS4 version).

# Video Requirements

*These rules apply for categories and levels that require video evidence (specified in the category rules):*

- The video cannot have any information (such as bottle count, coin count, PS3 clock etc.) covered by other elements;
- Game sound must be audible;
- The video must have a permanently hosted link (preferably YouTube). Videos hosted on Twitch are not accepted due to their storage limit.

Top (~5) runs will be held to an even higher standard.

*Tip: If you want to play music on your stream, try recording locally with OBS without recording the music. The past broadcast on Twitch would likely be muted and thus unusable for submissions. Reach out in the Sly Cooper Speedruns Discord if you need help to set this up.*

# Emulator Rules 

The use of RPCS3 to emulate the remastered (PS3) version is allowed, but emulator runs may not claim a time among the Top 40% of the total number of leaderboard placements in a category.

- RPCS3 version 0.0.29 or newer must be used;
- The game must not be modified in any way, either through modifying the game files or externally manipulating the game via a program such as Cheat Engine;
- Performance Overlay must be turned on in Config -> Emulator -> Enable performance overlay. You must show at least Minimal detail to display the FPS counter. You may customize the overlay, but it must show FPS at all times during the run and shouldn't cover any information such as coin count;
- You may change the system language, but changing any other emulator settings during the run is not permitted;
- Rebooting the game must be done by either using the Home Menu, clicking File -> Boot Game, or right-clicking the game on the game list and selecting Reboot;
- The use of savestates is not permitted during the run;
- You must set the framerate cap to 60fps. Use of other framerate caps such as 50fps or 30fps is prohibited;
- You may toggle PPU Non-Java Mode Fixup (in Advanced settings) to prevent unexpected bottle crashes and incorrect renders.
- You may change the Resolution Scale slider to one that makes the game look better.

# Gamepad Rules 

Macro modifications for controllers or the use of a Turbo mode are banned. Aesthetic controller mods, carving the controller shell, removing functionality (e.g. rumble), replacing OEM controller parts, and adapters allowing unofficial controllers are allowed.

If remapping a controller layout through use of an adapter, PS4/PS5 settings, console modifications, or emulator, face buttons may only be mapped to other face buttons, triggers to triggers, and sticks to sticks. Double mapping (having more than one of the same input, for example: two X buttons) is banned. Remapping during the run is banned. Additional buttons and paddles not present on the original console's controller (e.g. Xbox Elite controller's back paddles) are banned.

External devices for analog/digital inputs (other than the controller itself) are banned.

